  "recipe": {
    "technique": "The craft uses the leaves of the screw pine (Pandanus), a shrub that grows wild along the rivers, canals, ponds and backwaters of Kerala and is also planted as a natural fence. The plant is called thazha or kaitha in Malayalam, and a woven screw pine mat is known as thazhappaya. Only mature leaves are cut from the plant. Their thorny edges are trimmed off, and each leaf is split lengthwise into thin strips. The strips are boiled and washed to lighten them, soaked in fresh water, and then dried in the sun until they turn a pale ivory colour. They are straightened with a knife, rolled into bundles, and some are dyed before weaving."
  },
